Artemis the Ranger schrieb:
> 
> Quick question about the Ranger Quest Artifact. I got through the
> quest on my first try ever (killing Scorpius in three moves with my
> /oF, while he sat on the up stair several squares away watching me!
> Stupidest quest nemesis I've ever seen)

Oh, quest nemeses are always a bit stupid that way, the stair-hugging
buggers. Scipio can be rather troublesome when he decides to fight you
for a change. If you fail to pay attention he'll smack you good and
proper and sow your grave with salt[1].

> On my third or fourth invocation of the Longbow to get more arrows, I
> got the following message: "You feel that the Longbow of Diana is
> ignoring you."
> 
> (1) Why is this happening? I've checked through the spoilers and
> haven't been able to find any reference to this at all.

The last invocation just wasn't long enough ago. The invocation code
uses a timeout function similar to prayer timeouts; the number of
turns a quest artefact takes to "charge up" is variable - most of the
time it's something like 200-400 turns or so, but occasionally you'll
get a rotten roll of the dice and it'll take nigh on a thousand turns.

> (2) Will the Longbow ever *stop* ignoring me, or have I used up my
> supply of ammo for the game? (Horrible thought...)

It will come back on-line, but you'll have to wait until it stops
sulking. Invoking an artefact when it's not ready not only denies you
the invocation effect, it also increases the remaining "time to
recharge" some more. Basically, don't keep trying every dozen turns,
only try every two hundred turns or so.

> (3) Is there any way to tell when this is going to happen?

No. The game doesn't tell you whether an artefact is ready to be
invoked again.

